## Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Next.js 14 project.

### What was implemented:

1. **Fetched Latest Documentation**
   - Retrieved the most recent installation instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
   - Identified Next.js-specific integration requirements

2. **Package Installation**
   - Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` v2.1.0 package
   - Added the package as a dependency in package.json

3. **Speed Insights Integration**
   - Modified `src/app/layout.tsx` to import SpeedInsights component from `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
   - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component at the end of the body tag in the root layout
   - Placement ensures the component loads after all other page content

4. **ESLint Configuration**
   - Set up ESLint with Next.js configuration for proper code quality checking
   - Installed ESLint v8.57.1 and eslint-config-next v14.2.35 (compatible with Next.js 14)
   - Created `.eslintrc.json` with recommended Next.js configuration
   - Verified no linting errors were introduced by the changes

5. **Build Verification**
   - Successfully built the project with Next.js build command
   - All pages compiled correctly (10 routes generated)
   - No TypeScript or build errors introduced

### Files Modified:
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights import and component
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency and ESLint dev dependencies
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package information

### Files Created:
- `.eslintrc.json` - ESLint configuration for Next.js

### Implementation Details:

The SpeedInsights component was added following the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router:
- Imported from `@vercel/speed-insights/next` (Next.js-specific package)
- Placed inside the body tag but outside all provider contexts
- This placement ensures Speed Insights tracks all page navigations and performance metrics

The implementation is minimal and non-intrusive, preserving all existing functionality while adding performance monitoring capabilities. Speed Insights will automatically start collecting Core Web Vitals and other performance metrics once the application is deployed to Vercel.

### Testing:
- ✓ Build completed successfully
- ✓ Linter verified (no errors in modified files)
- ✓ No TypeScript errors
- ✓ All existing functionality preserved

The Speed Insights integration is now ready and will begin collecting performance data when the site receives traffic after deployment.
